li='Decision panel | Cutoff: November 27, 2026, 6:36 a.m. CST (12:36 UTC)\n\n1. AI — Marlin adds research modes (Sakana AI, Nov. 26). FACT: Twilight/Midnight 2.0 and redesigned slides; new modes consume 300 credits versus Sunlight’s 100. INFERENCE: Benchmark accuracy, time and cost. UNCERTAINTY: Vendor quality claims, unverified independently.\nhttps://sakana.ai/marlin-update-2/\n\n2. QUANT — News embeddings face memory bias (preprint submitted Nov. 24; listed Nov. 26). FACT: Event-category baselines outperform short-horizon embedding forecasts; earlier firm coverage explains longer-horizon predictability. INFERENCE: Test encoders whose training ends before evaluation. UNCERTAINTY: Memory attribution is model-dependent; unreplicated.\nhttps://arxiv.org/html/2611.33458v1\n\n3. MARKETS — Futures rebound (Reuters, Nov. 27). FACT: At 1:13 a.m. CST, Dow/S&P/Nasdaq 100 E-minis were +0.89%/+1.65%/+2.47%. INFERENCE: Recheck QQQ/SPY opening liquidity. UNCERTAINTY: Early reported snapshot, not live executable ETF returns or proof of reversal.\nhttps://www.reuters.com/business/wall-st-futures-surge-investors-return-holiday-2026-11-27/\n\n4. ECONOMY — GDP revised up (BEA, Nov. 25). FACT: Q3 real GDP annualized growth 4.3%, versus 3.4% advance estimate. INFERENCE: Stress rate/growth exposures and preserve vintage data. UNCERTAINTY: Further revisions and Fed response unknown.\nhttps://www.bea.gov/news/2026/gdp-second-estimate-and-corporate-profits-3rd-quarter-2026\n\n5. BUSINESS — Black Friday demand test (Reuters, Nov. 27 UTC). FACT: Holiday-spending forecasts point to 4%–6% growth despite shaky sentiment. INFERENCE: Separate nominal sales from units and margins. UNCERTAINTY: Forecasts, not realized Black Friday sales.\nhttps://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/cautious-consumers-gear-up-black-friday-inflation-woes-bite-2026-11-27/\n\nVOLATILITY / EXECUTION: High, medium confidence; Nov. 25 prior-close VIX 28.29 (YCharts). Cash opens 8:30 a.m., closes noon CST today; eligible options 12:15 p.m., subject to contract/venue. Spreads, depth, volume, funding and gamma unverified. Use fresh quotes and staged limits; stress opening/closing auctions, partial fills and stale options. Factor returns/rankings unavailable: comparable publication-cleared data unresolved; intended Nov. 24–25 and Oct. 28–Nov. 25 windows.\n\nMATLAB / DRL: Independent capital-preservation gates, net-cost rewards and purged regime holdouts. Align timetables, profile first, preserve random streams and trial order. Audit leakage, survivorship, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options, multiple testing, calibration and drift.\n\nRESEARCH QUESTION: Does a point-in-time news embedding beat an event-category baseline after costs? Worth testing because pretraining memory can contaminate backtests.\n\nFull dashboard and five graphics: https://github.com/rsh63/market-state-lab/blob/main/2026-11-27.md\n\nResearch and education, not individualized financial advice.\n\nWould you require a pretraining cutoff before every evaluation date, or also anonymize firm identity?\nSubscribe by email: https://market-state-lab.ghost.io/?utm_source=linkedin&utm_medium=social&utm_campaign=qmb_2026-11-27#/portal/signup'
